      "problem": "Find the sum $1 - \\dfrac{9}{2!} + \\dfrac{81}{4!}-\\cdots + \\dfrac{(-1)^{n}3^{2n}}{(2n)!} \\,\\cdots \\,.$",
      "worked_solution": "We recognize that the series looks similar to the Maclaurin expansion for $f(x) = \\cos x.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=1-\\frac{1}{2!}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{4!}{x}^{4}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{x}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=3$ into our Maclaurin expansion gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3) & =1-\\frac{{3}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{3}^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}{3}^{2n}}{(2n)!}\\,⋯ \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3) & =1-\\frac{9}{2!}+\\frac{81}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}{3}^{2n}}{(2n)!}\\,⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the series is $\\cos(3).$",
